#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166521 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf357ee2-b8b4-538c-b269-f7546cf5374f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Coordinates Relative to a Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "4dac81da-f15c-55ff-9630-7349a3e03e57" :question/math-academy-id "e-8273" :question/problem "Consider the polynomials $p_1(t)$ and $p_2(t)$, given by\n$p_1(t)=3+2t, \\qquad p_2(t)=-t+t^2$.\nFind $p(t)$ given that $\\mathcal{B}=\\big\\{p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{p_1, p_2 \\big\\}$, and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{p_1, p_2 \\big\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\nx_{1}p_{1}(t) + x_{2}p_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np(t) &= 4 \\cdot (3 + 2t) + (-3) \\cdot (-t + t^{2}) \\\\\n&= 12 + 8t + 3t - 3t^{2} \\\\\n&= 12 + 11t - 3t^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166522 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/id #uuid "aac4b559-b26b-57b0-8701-b3235969cd2f" :question/math-academy-id "e-8274" :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\nIf $\\mathcal B = \\{B_1,B_2\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{B_1, B_2 \\}$, calculate $\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that\n\n$$\nx_1 B_1 +x_2 B_2 = A\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix} + x_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x_{1} - x_{2} & 0 \\\\ 8x_{1} - 2x_{2} & -4x_{1} + x_{2}\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{2x_{1} - x_{2} =-5; 8x_{1} - 2x_{2} =-2; - 4x_{1} + x_{2} = 1\n$$\n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nM = \\mid \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-4)R_{1} \\\\ R_{3}:=R_{3} + 2R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\end{vmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 18 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{2x_{1} - x_{2} =-5; 2x_{2} = 18; - x_{2} =-9\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get $x_2 =9$. From the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x_{1} - 9 &= -5 \\\\\n2x_{1} &= 4 \\\\\nx_{1} &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166523 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d8f8be0-0fe9-5734-87d3-5c432b7f298f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Polynomial Vector Space"}] :question/id #uuid "f0fc412f-8276-5876-a509-4f2173396e72" :question/math-academy-id "e-8275" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$p_1(t)=5+t^2, \\quad p_2(t)=3t-2t^2, \\quad q(t)=5-3t+3t^2$.\n\nIf $\\mathcal{B}=\\{p_1(t), p_2(t) \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\}$, find $[q(t)]_{\\mathcal{B}}$." :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that\n\n$$\nx_1 p_1(t)+x_2 p_2(t) = q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}(5 + t^{2}) + x_{2}(3t - 2t^{2}) &= 5 - 3t + 3t^{2} \\\\\n5x_{1} + 3x_{2}t + (x_{1} - 2x_{2})t^{2} &= 5 - 3t + 3t^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{5x_{1} = 5; 3x_{2} =-3; x_{1} - 2x_{2} = 3\n$$\n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nM =\\begin{vmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3} &:=R_{3} + (-\\frac{1}{5})R_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + \\frac{2}{3}R_{2}; ∼ \\mid \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{5x_{1} = 5; 3x_{2} =-3\n$$\n\nFrom the first and second equations, we get $x_1=1$ and $x_2 =-1$. Therefore, $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0a6b6e1-fb99-5ebe-9f3f-000878f79f0d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector With Respect to a Given Basis in a Matrix Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805a501b-a4fc-52a1-ac9f-33f7defa1351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165032} {:answer/id #uuid "e0858ade-2f58-56e3-8513-a3ba860887e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165033} {:answer/id #uuid "4afd8b98-e2ec-5e30-9eec-ac7582d8358b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165034} {:answer/id #uuid "4daedf73-e868-57d9-bff6-36c1fefb6a68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165035} {:answer/id #uuid "794e960d-3da4-5a66-93db-bbe39e9cd982" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 1759